# Design tokens

All visual values live in `tokens.css` (or `tokens.json` if your stack
consumes JSON). **Never inline a hex code, font family, px size, or
duration in component CSS.** If a value is missing, add it as a token
first, then consume it.

## Color tokens

| Token                  | Value                       | Use                                       |
| ---------------------- | --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `--color-bg`           | `#fafafa`                   | page background                           |
| `--color-fg`           | `#14151a`                   | body text, titles, masthead rule          |
| `--color-fg-muted`     | `#4a4f57`                   | blockquote body, sidebar links            |
| `--color-meta`         | `#6b6f78`                   | dateline, footer, archive date column     |
| `--color-rule`         | `rgba(20,21,26,0.12)`       | hairline dividers (post separators, etc.) |
| `--color-rule-strong`  | `#14151a`                   | 2px masthead underline                    |
| `--color-accent`       | `#d97757`                   | links, stars, wordmark dot, CTA hover     |
| `--color-accent-fg`    | `#ffffff`                   | foreground on solid-accent surfaces       |

## Typography tokens

```css
--font-mono:  'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo,
              Consolas, monospace;
--font-serif: 'Newsreader', 'Source Serif Pro', Georgia, serif;
```

Scale (do not introduce new sizes without a corresponding token):

```
body 17 / 1.6   wordmark 20   nav 12   title 18 / 1.3
h1 22 / 1.35    dateline 11   sidebar 12   cta 13
```

## Spacing scale

A 4px base. Use only these values:

```
4  8  12  16  20  24  32  40  44  48  56  80
```

Tokens: `--space-1` (4px) through `--space-20` (80px). No `13px`, no
`27px`, no "I just need a bit more" — pick the nearest token.

## Reviewer cue

If you see `color: #...` or `font-family: '...'` or a raw `padding: 13px`
in a diff, that is a smell. Replace with a token or add the token first.
